BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skiathos-skiathos-town-feast-of-the-finding-of-the-icon-of-panagia-ei-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270704
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270706
SUMMARY:Feast of the Finding of the Icon of Panagia Eikonistria\, Skiathos Town
LOCATION:Skiathos Town\, Skiathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Skiathos' second feast of its patroness marks the finding of the icon in a pine tree in 1655. On the evening of 4 July the icon is carried from Treis Ierarches to the church of Genniseos tis Theotokou for vespers with several bishops\, and on the morning of the 5th\, after the liturgy\, it is processed through the streets of the Chora. Pilgrims come from the mainland\, so the town churches are packed\; it is a religious event with no glenti attached.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#skiathos-town-feast-of-the-finding-of-the-icon-of-panagia-ei
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#skiathos-town-feast-of-the-finding-of-the-icon-of-panagia-ei
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:agistri-limenaria-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-limenaria-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270706
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270708
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Kyriaki\, Limenaria
LOCATION:Limenaria\, Agistri\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Limenaria\, the quiet old village at the south end of the island\, keeps Agia Kyriaki on 7 July with a liturgy and a small feast\; it is the most local of Agistri's three feasts and a good excuse to walk the pine road from Megalochori.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/agistri/#limenaria-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-limenaria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/agistri/#limenaria-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-limenaria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lefkada-vlycho-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-vlycho-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270706
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270708
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Kyriaki\, Vlycho
LOCATION:Vlycho\, Lefkada\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The chapel of Agia Kyriaki sits on the rock across the bay from Vlycho\, and the village's panigiri around her feast (6–7 July) has grown into the biggest folk-music night of the Lefkada summer\, with name clarinet players from Epirus and Aitoloakarnania booked each year and dancing on the waterfront until dawn. Held on or just before 7 July\; expect crowds from the mainland\, get there by 10pm and park on the Nydri road.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#vlycho-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-vlycho
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#vlycho-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-vlycho
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mykonos-mykonos-chora-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-mykonos-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270706
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270708
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Kyriaki\, Mykonos Chora
LOCATION:Mykonos Chora\, Mykonos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Mykonian panigiria are run by the families who own the chapels\, and Agia Kyriaki on 7 July is one of the few in town: vespers with artoklasia on the evening of the 6th\, then wine\, boiled lamb\, kremidopita and kopanisti for everyone\, with tsambouna and toumbaki and dancing into the night. Rural chapels at Mikres and Megales Diles celebrate the same saint the same night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#mykonos-chora-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-mykonos-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#mykonos-chora-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-mykonos-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:samos-koumaradaioi-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-koumaradaioi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270706
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270708
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Kyriaki\, Koumaradaioi
LOCATION:Koumaradaioi\, Samos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:At the chapel of Agia Kyriaki on the edge of Koumaradaioi\, on the road to Pyrgos\, the village's church-and-volunteer-firefighters association stages a feast on the evening of 6 July with an island-music orchestra in the church courtyard and the road outside\, souvlaki\, paspalas (the local pork-and-egg dish)\, pancakes and salads\; liturgy and refreshments follow on the morning of the 7th. A classic inland Samos panigiri\, 20 minutes from Pythagoreio.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#koumaradaioi-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-koumaradaioi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#koumaradaioi-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-koumaradaioi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:elafonisos-elafonisos-liberation-anniversary-and-agios-spyridon-process-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270709
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270713
SUMMARY:Liberation anniversary and Agios Spyridon procession\, Elafonisos
LOCATION:Elafonisos\, Elafonisos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Elafonisos celebrates its union with Greece (6 July 1850) and the consecration of its harbour church together: bells and flags on the 6th\, and on the 9th a hierarchical liturgy with the Metropolitan of Monemvasia and Sparta followed by a procession of the icon of Agios Spyridon around the harbour with children in costume\, then cultural performances on the harbour square in the evening. Early July is quieter and cheaper than August on the island.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/elafonisos/#elafonisos-liberation-anniversary-and-agios-spyridon-process
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/elafonisos/#elafonisos-liberation-anniversary-and-agios-spyridon-process
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sifnos-vathy-panigiri-of-taxiarchis-vathy-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270712
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270714
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Taxiarchis\, Vathy
LOCATION:Vathy\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Vathy's whitewashed Taxiarchis monastery right on the beach celebrates twice a year\; the summer feast is on the evening of 12 July (Synaxis of Archangel Gabriel)\, with vespers\, then revithada and braised lamb at the monastery tables and a violin-and-laouto takimi. Same night the chapel of Ai-Silivestros on the Cheronissos road also celebrates. The village has a small car park\; many people come by boat from Kamares.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#vathy-panigiri-of-taxiarchis-vathy
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#vathy-panigiri-of-taxiarchis-vathy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mathraki-mathraki-panigiri-of-the-miracle-of-agios-spyridon-mathraki-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270713
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270714
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the miracle of Agios Spyridon\, Mathraki
LOCATION:Mathraki\, Mathraki\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Mathraki's one big night is the 13 July feast of the miracle of Agios Spyridon (also linked locally to a sight-restoring miracle of Agios Theodoros)\, organised by the Diapolos cultural association with live music and food in the village\; in 2022 it was held on Thursday 14 July\, so the date shifts a day for the boat. A free boat leaves Agios Stefanos (Corfu) at 5pm and returns after midnight\, weather permitting — ring the association to confirm.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mathraki/#mathraki-panigiri-of-the-miracle-of-agios-spyridon-mathraki
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mathraki/#mathraki-panigiri-of-the-miracle-of-agios-spyridon-mathraki
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-naxos-chora-feast-of-agios-nikodimos-patron-of-naxos-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270713
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270715
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Nikodimos\, patron of Naxos\, Chora
LOCATION:Naxos Chora\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:St Nikodimos the Hagiorite was born in Naxos town and is the island's patron: on the evening of 13 July there is a multi-bishop vespers at his church in Chora\, on the 14th the liturgy\, and in the evening the procession of his icon and relics through the streets of the town with the band and the authorities. Religious rather than a food panigiri\, but the town is at its most festive.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#naxos-chora-feast-of-agios-nikodimos-patron-of-naxos-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#naxos-chora-feast-of-agios-nikodimos-patron-of-naxos-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:evia-central-steni-feast-of-agioi-kirykos-and-ioulitta-ano-steni-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270714
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270716
SUMMARY:Feast of Agioi Kirykos and Ioulitta\, Ano Steni
LOCATION:Steni\, Evia (Central)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Steni\, the plane-tree village at the foot of Dirfys\, keeps 15 July at its chapel of Agioi Kirykos and Ioulitta with a liturgy (the Metropolitan of Chalkida presided in 2018) and a breakfast laid on by the parish council afterwards\; the same village hosts a municipal trade fair (emporopanigyri) at the end of August. Cool mountain air and tavernas on the stream make it a pleasant July escape from Chalkida.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-central/#steni-feast-of-agioi-kirykos-and-ioulitta-ano-steni
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-central/#steni-feast-of-agioi-kirykos-and-ioulitta-ano-steni
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-exo-plagia-panigiri-of-agios-kirykos-agia-ioulitta-exo-plagi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270716
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Kirykos & Agia Ioulitta\, Exo Plagia
LOCATION:Exo Plagia\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island capital's own feast\, for its patron saints Kirykos and Ioulitta — the warm-up to Ikaria's big mid-summer run. Tables fill the square\, the wine is from the barrel\, and the Ikariotiko dancing builds long past midnight.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#exo-plagia-panigiri-of-agios-kirykos-agia-ioulitta-exo-plagi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#exo-plagia-panigiri-of-agios-kirykos-agia-ioulitta-exo-plagi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aegina-agia-marina-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agia-marina-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Agia Marina
LOCATION:Agia Marina\, Aegina\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The resort of Agia Marina on the east coast takes its name from the church\, and on the evening of 16 July\, after vespers\, the Oinoi cultural association's dance groups perform and a traditional glenti open to all follows\, with food and live music. It is the beach-town panigiri of the island\; buses from Aegina town run late that night\, or stay over and swim in the morning.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/aegina/#agia-marina-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agia-marina
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/aegina/#agia-marina-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agia-marina
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:andros-apoikia-panigiri-of-agia-marina-monastery-apoikia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina monastery\, Apoikia
LOCATION:Apoikia\, Andros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The monastery of Agia Marina above the spring village of Apoikia\, north of Chora\, is Andros's big pilgrimage of the summer: a vigil on the night of 16 July and the liturgy on the 17th draw thousands\, and the monks offer food to pilgrims. Palaiopoli on the west coast keeps a village feast for the same saint\, with house-to-house visits and instruments. Park below the monastery and walk the last stretch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#apoikia-panigiri-of-agia-marina-monastery-apoikia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#apoikia-panigiri-of-agia-marina-monastery-apoikia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:antiparos-antiparos-chora-three-day-feast-of-agia-marina-antiparos-har-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270719
SUMMARY:Three-day feast of Agia Marina\, Antiparos harbour
LOCATION:Antiparos (Chora)\, Antiparos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Antiparos turns the feast of Agia Marina (17 July) into a three-day harbour festival around 15-17 July: a sailing race\, a swim and a street run in the days before\, then the icon procession on the 17th\, prize-giving for the athletes\, dancing\, songs and kerasmata on the quay. It is the island's main summer event\, so book a room if you want to stay over.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/antiparos/#antiparos-chora-three-day-feast-of-agia-marina-antiparos-har
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/antiparos/#antiparos-chora-three-day-feast-of-agia-marina-antiparos-har
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:corfu-benitses-panigiri-of-agia-marina-benitses-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Benitses
LOCATION:Benitses\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Benitses celebrates Agia Marina over two nights\, 16 and 17 July\, with a litany of the icon through the village and live traditional music on the harbour square\, food from the local associations and dancing. Agia Marina is also kept in Spartera\, Avliotes and Karousades the same night if you are in the north.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#benitses-panigiri-of-agia-marina-benitses
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#benitses-panigiri-of-agia-marina-benitses
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:folegandros-agali-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agali-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Agali
LOCATION:Agali\, Folegandros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The beach hamlet of Agali celebrates its Agia Marina on the evening of 16 July: vespers\, then food and wine offered by the families and violin-and-laouto music with the locals leading the dances. It's the first of the island's summer panigiria and small enough that everyone ends up in the same circle. Take the bus down from Chora — the road is steep and parking at Agali is scarce.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#agali-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agali
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#agali-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agali
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:heraklion-voni-panigiri-and-pilgrimage-of-agia-marina-voni-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri and pilgrimage of Agia Marina\, Voni
LOCATION:Voni\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The monastery of Agia Marina at Voni in the Pediada is Crete's main Agia Marina pilgrimage: from the evening of 16 July queues of pilgrims stretch out of the two churches (the tiny old one and the big new one)\, people sleep in the courtyard to fulfil vows\, and stalls and a glenti fill the road outside. Come on the eve for the atmosphere\; the morning liturgy on the 17th is packed and parking is a kilometre away on the Kastelli road.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#voni-panigiri-and-pilgrimage-of-agia-marina-voni
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#voni-panigiri-and-pilgrimage-of-agia-marina-voni
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ithaca-exogi-panigiri-of-agia-marina-exogi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Exogi
LOCATION:Exogi\, Ithaca\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Exogi is the highest village on Ithaca\, and its panigiri for Agia Marina fills the small square with its huge view over the north of the island: service in the evening\, then food\, wine and live music with dancing that often goes to sunrise. The road up from Stavros is narrow with hairpins\; go up before dark and park at the entrance to the village.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#exogi-panigiri-of-agia-marina-exogi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#exogi-panigiri-of-agia-marina-exogi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:karpathos-menetes-panigiri-of-agia-marina-menetes-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Menetes
LOCATION:Menetes\, Karpathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Menetes\, the amphitheatre village above Pigadia\, feasts Agia Marina on 16-17 July with a glendi of Karpathian music and free food after the vespers. The same village runs the Agios Ioannis feast at Afiarti on 29 August. Ten minutes from Pigadia\; there is a small folklore museum worth seeing while you are there.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#menetes-panigiri-of-agia-marina-menetes
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#menetes-panigiri-of-agia-marina-menetes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kasos-agia-marina-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agia-marina-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Agia Marina
LOCATION:Agia Marina\, Kasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The largest village on Kasos feasts its namesake saint on 16-17 July with a glendi of lyra and laouto\, free wine and food on the square. Agia Marina also hosts the Transfiguration (6 August) and Holy Cross (14 September) feasts. Fifteen minutes' walk uphill from Fry.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#agia-marina-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agia-marina
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#agia-marina-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agia-marina
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-merichas-panigiri-of-agia-marina-merichas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Merichas
LOCATION:Merichas\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The port's summer feast at the chapel of Agia Marina in Merichas\, on the evening of 16 July\, with a glenti with island violin and laouto after vespers\; the Agia Marina at Lefkes celebrates the same night. It's the easiest Kythnos panigiri to reach — you can walk from the ferry — and the harbour tavernas stay open late for it.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#merichas-panigiri-of-agia-marina-merichas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#merichas-panigiri-of-agia-marina-merichas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lemnos-androni-panigiri-of-agia-marina-androni-park-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Androni park
LOCATION:Androni\, Lemnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 'Argonautes' club of Androni\, just outside Myrina\, opens the Lemnos panigiri season with Agia Marina on the evening of 16 July in the village park\, and repeats the formula for Agios Panteleimon on 26 July with a full Lemnian orchestra (Mavrakis family violins in 2026). Souvlaki\, local wine and island dances\; ten minutes from Myrina by car. Nea Koutali and Livadochori also keep Agia Marina with church feasts.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#androni-panigiri-of-agia-marina-androni-park
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#androni-panigiri-of-agia-marina-androni-park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leros-agia-marina-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agia-marina-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Agia Marina
LOCATION:Agia Marina\, Leros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The patron feast of Leros' capital: on the evening of 16 July the metropolitan leads a grand vespers at the 1933 church\, then the icon is carried through the lanes down to the harbour with the municipal band\, and the party continues in the cafes along the waterfront\; liturgy and a reception with local sweets on the 17th. Stay in Agia Marina or Platanos so you can walk.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/leros/#agia-marina-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agia-marina
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/leros/#agia-marina-panigiri-of-agia-marina-agia-marina
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-triovasalos-panigiri-of-agia-marina-triovasalos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Triovasalos
LOCATION:Triovasalos\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 16 July the Triovasalos beautification society throws a free glenti in the courtyard of Agia Marina from 21:30\, with live traditional musicians (violin\, laouto\, vocals) and dancing until late. The chapel of Agia Marina at Chalakas holds its own smaller feast the same evening straight after vespers\, so locals often hop between the two. Park on the main Adamas–Plaka road and walk in\; the village lanes fill up.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#triovasalos-panigiri-of-agia-marina-triovasalos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#triovasalos-panigiri-of-agia-marina-triovasalos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-koronos-panigiri-of-agia-marina-koronos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Koronos
LOCATION:Koronos\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Koronos\, the emery-miners' village stacked up a ravine in the north-east\, throws its big feast for Agia Marina on 16-17 July: revithada from the wood oven\, rooster in wine sauce\, local wine\, and Koronos's own violin-and-laouto tradition until dawn. The road from Chora is 45 minutes of bends\; park where the tarmac widens above the village and walk down the steps.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#koronos-panigiri-of-agia-marina-koronos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#koronos-panigiri-of-agia-marina-koronos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paros-kostos-panigiri-of-agia-marina-kostos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Kostos
LOCATION:Kostos\, Paros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kostos\, the small hill village between Parikia and Lefkes\, keeps the Agia Marina feast on 16-17 July: vespers on the eve\, then tables in the square with food from the village association and violin-and-laouto dancing. It is one of the few proper mountain-village panigiria on Paros and much less touristy than anything in Naoussa. Park on the main road below the village and walk up.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#kostos-panigiri-of-agia-marina-kostos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#kostos-panigiri-of-agia-marina-kostos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rhodes-paradisi-panigiri-of-agia-marina-paradisi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Paradisi
LOCATION:Paradisi\, Rhodes\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Paradisi\, the village just past the airport\, holds the island's best-known Agia Marina feast on 16-17 July: vespers and procession on the eve\, then the square fills with tables\, souvlaki and a live band until late. Apolakia in the south does its own Agia Marina on the 16th. Easy to reach by the airport bus\; go on the evening of the 16th for the party.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#paradisi-panigiri-of-agia-marina-paradisi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#paradisi-panigiri-of-agia-marina-paradisi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sifnos-flambouro-apollonia-area-panigiri-of-agia-marina-flambouro-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Flambouro
LOCATION:Flambouro (Apollonia area)\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Agia Marina that Sifniots go to is the chapel at Flambouro\, behind Profitis Ilias Apsilos: vespers and a morning panigiri on 17 July\, with the usual chickpea soup and lamb from the panigyras. Kamares (18 July) and Vathy (19 July) hold their own smaller Agia Marina feasts on the following nights\, so you can catch one each evening. It's reached on foot from the Apollonia–Profitis Ilias path\; wear proper shoes.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#flambouro-apollonia-area-panigiri-of-agia-marina-flambouro
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#flambouro-apollonia-area-panigiri-of-agia-marina-flambouro
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:spetses-agia-marina-feast-of-agia-marina-agia-marina-beach-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Feast of Agia Marina\, Agia Marina beach
LOCATION:Agia Marina\, Spetses\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The chapel above Agia Marina beach\, a 20-minute walk east of the Old Harbour\, keeps 17 July with vespers on the eve and a liturgy on the day\, and the beach bars below take the overflow. Small and mostly for the locals\; combine it with a swim.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#agia-marina-feast-of-agia-marina-agia-marina-beach
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#agia-marina-feast-of-agia-marina-agia-marina-beach
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:symi-agia-marina-islet-panigiri-of-agia-marina-islet-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina islet
LOCATION:Agia Marina islet\, Symi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Boats shuttle from Pedi and Gialos to the chapel islet of Agia Marina off Symi's north-east tip for vespers on 16 July and a feast on the islet with fried fish and wine. One of the prettiest panigiri settings in the Dodecanese\; go over before sunset.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/symi/#agia-marina-islet-panigiri-of-agia-marina-islet
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/symi/#agia-marina-islet-panigiri-of-agia-marina-islet
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fournoi-fournoi-panigiri-of-agia-marina-fournoi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270717
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Fournoi
LOCATION:Fournoi\, Fournoi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The first summer panigiri of Fournoi: liturgy at the chapel of Agia Marina in the Varela area\, then from about 21:00 the cultural association takes over the village square with live island music\, goat\, mezedes and wine. The whole island turns up\, so arrive early for a table.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/fournoi/#fournoi-panigiri-of-agia-marina-fournoi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/fournoi/#fournoi-panigiri-of-agia-marina-fournoi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-agios-kirykos-agia-marina-panigiri-17-july-liberation-annive-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270717
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Agia Marina panigiri & 17 July liberation anniversary\, Agios Kirykos
LOCATION:Agios Kirykos\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The capital's big day: 17 July is both Agia Marina and the anniversary of the 1912 Ikarian uprising\, so there is a morning doxology and parade\, then in the evening the PAS Ikaros club runs a panigiri on the marina with an Ikarian orchestra (Marios and company in recent years). Expect goat\, wine by the kilo and the ikariotikos danced in long chains until late. Ferries and rooms in town fill for this weekend\; walk in\, there is no parking near the harbour.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#agios-kirykos-agia-marina-panigiri-17-july-liberation-annive
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#agios-kirykos-agia-marina-panigiri-17-july-liberation-annive
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-arethousa-panigiri-of-agia-marina-arethousa-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270717
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Arethousa
LOCATION:Arethousa\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The quieter alternative to the capital's 17 July: a traditional day panigiri in the mountain village of Arethousa above Evdilos\, starting after the liturgy and running through the afternoon with goat\, wine and violin. Smaller crowd\, more locals\, more room to dance. Katafygi near Agios Kirykos holds its Agia Marina feast the evening before (16 July).\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#arethousa-panigiri-of-agia-marina-arethousa
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#arethousa-panigiri-of-agia-marina-arethousa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kea-otzias-otzias-festival-agia-marina-otzias-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270717
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Otzias festival (Agia Marina)\, Otzias
LOCATION:Otzias\, Kea (Tzia)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 'Giorti tou Otzia'\, co-organised by the municipality and the local society on 17 July (Agia Marina's day) from 20:00 on the waterfront: food from the village associations\, live island music and dancing by the sea. The bay's tavernas are the fallback for dinner if the queues get long\; it's a 15-minute drive from Korissia.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kea/#otzias-otzias-festival-agia-marina-otzias
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kea/#otzias-otzias-festival-agia-marina-otzias
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-angeria-panigiri-of-agios-aimilianos-angeria-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270717
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270719
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Aimilianos\, Angeria
LOCATION:Angeria\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Angeria\, the farming village on the road to Paliochori\, celebrates its Agios Aimilianos with vespers at 20:00 on 17 July followed by a courtyard glenti with violin and laouto players from the island\, and liturgy at 07:00 next morning. A canteen sells local food and drink\, so come hungry\; it's a low-key\, mostly local affair — a good pick if you find the Adamas feasts too busy.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#angeria-panigiri-of-agios-aimilianos-angeria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#angeria-panigiri-of-agios-aimilianos-angeria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:samothrace-alonia-panigiri-of-agia-marina-alonia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270717
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Alonia
LOCATION:Alonia\, Samothrace\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The first of Samothrace's summer panigiria\, in the farming village of Alonia below Chora\, organised by the island's cultural association 'Saos'. After the morning liturgy the village serves the Samothracian classic\, gorgovrasto (quick-boiled goat)\, and there is dancing to local music. Simple\, cheap and genuinely local.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samothrace/#alonia-panigiri-of-agia-marina-alonia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samothrace/#alonia-panigiri-of-agia-marina-alonia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:corfu-magoulades-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-magoulades-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Profitis Ilias\, Magoulades
LOCATION:Magoulades\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Magoulades\, in the hills of the north-west behind Arillas\, is the Corfu village that celebrates Profitis Ilias\, with vespers on the 19th and a panigiri in the square with a Corfiot orchestra and tables of food\; Perithia\, Dragotina and Kalafationes also keep the day. It is a genuine inland village night\, ten minutes from the Arillas and Agios Stefanos beaches.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#magoulades-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-magoulades
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#magoulades-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-magoulades
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ithaca-kioni-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-kioni-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Profitis Ilias\, Kioni
LOCATION:Kioni\, Ithaca\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kioni's chapel of Profitis Ilias is built on a rock at the water's edge\, so villagers arrive for the liturgy in small fishing boats\, and the party afterwards is on the beach with a live orchestra playing beside the sea. It is one of the prettiest settings for a panigiri anywhere in the Ionian\; Kioni is tiny\, so book a room well ahead or drive over from Vathy (40 min).\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#kioni-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-kioni
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#kioni-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-kioni
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:koufonisia-pano-koufonisi-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Profitis Ilias
LOCATION:Pano Koufonisi\, Koufonisia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The chapel of Profitis Ilias on the island's low summit celebrates on 19-20 July with vespers and an island glenti afterwards: food\, wine and violins. Small and easy to reach on foot from the village.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/koufonisia/#pano-koufonisi-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/koufonisia/#pano-koufonisi-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lesvos-pelopi-three-day-horse-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-pelopi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270722
SUMMARY:Three-day horse panigiri of Profitis Ilias\, Pelopi
LOCATION:Pelopi\, Lesvos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Pelopi\, a horse-breeding village in the north-east\, makes Profitis Ilias a three-day affair (18-20 July) with a mounted parade\, horse 'beauty' contests\, traditional food and music. Profitis Ilias is also kept with a bull procession and kiskek in Agiasos\, a horseback pilgrimage in Skalochori and dancing in Vatera. If horses are your thing\, Pelopi is the one.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#pelopi-three-day-horse-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-pelopi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#pelopi-three-day-horse-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-pelopi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-chalakas-profitis-ilias-feast-chalakas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Profitis Ilias feast\, Chalakas
LOCATION:Chalakas\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Milos has several hilltop Profitis Ilias chapels\; the ones at Chalakas and Tramythia (and Komia) are the ones that actually celebrate\, with vespers on the evening of 19 July and a small glenti with island musicians at Chalakas. It's a chapel feast rather than a village square party — bring a jumper for the breeze and a torch for the dirt track back to the car.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#chalakas-profitis-ilias-feast-chalakas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#chalakas-profitis-ilias-feast-chalakas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:samos-pandroso-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-on-the-summit-of-karvoun-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Profitis Ilias on the summit of Karvounis (Ampelos)
LOCATION:Pandroso\, Samos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Pandroso cultural association 'Agios Dimitrios' hosts a two-day feast at the chapel on the 1\,150 m summit of Mount Karvounis (Ampelos): vespers on the evening of 19 July followed by a glendi with violin and laouto\, mezedes and drink just below the peak\, camping allowed overnight\, then liturgy and a communal meal on the 20th. Drive to Pandroso and follow the track\; bring warm clothes and a torch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#pandroso-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-on-the-summit-of-karvoun
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#pandroso-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-on-the-summit-of-karvoun
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:santorini-pyrgos-feast-of-profitis-ilias-monastery-pyrgos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Feast of Profitis Ilias monastery\, Pyrgos
LOCATION:Pyrgos\, Santorini\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The monastery of Profitis Ilias on Santorini's highest point above Pyrgos celebrates on 19-20 July with a vespers on the eve and the liturgy on the day\, followed by kerasmata for pilgrims and a panigiri down in Pyrgos with local wine\, food and music. The road up is narrow and parking at the top is scarce\; go early or walk up from Pyrgos.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#pyrgos-feast-of-profitis-ilias-monastery-pyrgos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#pyrgos-feast-of-profitis-ilias-monastery-pyrgos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:serifos-vounia-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-vounia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Profitis Ilias\, Vounia
LOCATION:Vounia\, Serifos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Profitis Ilias is celebrated at the chapels of Vounia and Xero Chorio in the island's interior on the evening of 19 July\, with the classic Serifos panigiri table — fava with olives and onion\, boiled goat with potatoes\, pasta with goat stew — and wine that doesn't stop. Some years there's a live violin\; ask in Chora. These are hamlet feasts with no facilities\, so eat what's offered and bring water.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#vounia-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-vounia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#vounia-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-vounia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sifnos-profitis-ilias-summit-above-apollonia-katavati-panigiri-of-p-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Profitis Ilias Apsilos (mountaintop monastery)
LOCATION:Profitis Ilias summit\, above Apollonia/Katavati\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Pilgrimage on foot to the highest point of the island (680m)\, where a small chapel sits on the summit. Locals walk up before dawn.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#profitis-ilias-summit-above-apollonia-katavati-panigiri-of-p
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#profitis-ilias-summit-above-apollonia-katavati-panigiri-of-p
