BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:samothrace-profitis-ilias-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-profitis-ilias-vil-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Profitis Ilias\, Profitis Ilias village
LOCATION:Profitis Ilias\, Samothrace\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The mountain village of Profitis Ilias in the south-west\, famous for its goat tavernas\, keeps its patron's day on 20 July with gorgovrasto after the liturgy\, dancing\, and roast goat in the evening. The island's best-known panigiri for food\; the tavernas are packed\, so eat at the communal tables or book.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samothrace/#profitis-ilias-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-profitis-ilias-vil
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samothrace/#profitis-ilias-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-profitis-ilias-vil
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chios-volissos-pilgrimage-feast-of-agia-markella-volissos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270721
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270723
SUMMARY:Pilgrimage feast of Agia Markella\, Volissos
LOCATION:Volissos\, Chios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The feast of Chios's patron saint at her seaside shrine and monastery below Volissos in the Amani region is the island's biggest religious event: thousands walk the roughly 50 km from Chios town overnight on 21 July\, sleep on the beach and attend the liturgy on the 22nd\, visiting the rocks where holy water springs. The municipality issues walking guidelines each year (left side of the road\, torch\, water) and bans wild camping\; drive slowly\, the road is full of pilgrims\, and refuel in Vrontados.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chios/#volissos-pilgrimage-feast-of-agia-markella-volissos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chios/#volissos-pilgrimage-feast-of-agia-markella-volissos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tinos-kechrovouni-monastery-chora-feast-of-agia-pelagia-and-the-pr-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270722
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270724
SUMMARY:Feast of Agia Pelagia and the procession to Kechrovouni
LOCATION:Kechrovouni monastery / Chora\, Tinos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 23 July Tinos remembers the vision of the nun Pelagia that led to the finding of the icon in 1823: after great vespers on the 22nd\, the icon of the Megalochari is driven up to the convent of Kechrovouni for the liturgy\, pilgrims picnic in the fields around the monastery\, and in the late afternoon the icon returns on foot in a procession that snakes 8 km down the mountain to Chora. Walk down with it\, but wear shoes for it and bring water.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/tinos/#kechrovouni-monastery-chora-feast-of-agia-pelagia-and-the-pr
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/tinos/#kechrovouni-monastery-chora-feast-of-agia-pelagia-and-the-pr
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hydra-profitis-ilias-vigil-of-agia-efpraxia-and-profitis-ilias-mon-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270724
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270726
SUMMARY:Vigil of Agia Efpraxia and Profitis Ilias monasteries\, above Hydra Town
LOCATION:Profitis Ilias\, Hydra\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The two monasteries on the mountain above the town\, Profitis Ilias (men) and Agia Efpraxia (women)\, sit side by side an hour's climb up the mule path. Agia Efpraxia keeps an all-night vigil on 24-25 July with the cathedral's choir and monastic refreshments in the refectory afterwards\; Profitis Ilias marks its own feast on 20 July. Go up in the late afternoon when the heat drops and come down by torchlight.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#profitis-ilias-vigil-of-agia-efpraxia-and-profitis-ilias-mon
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#profitis-ilias-vigil-of-agia-efpraxia-and-profitis-ilias-mon
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kefalonia-lakithra-livathos-panigiri-of-agia-anna-lakithra-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270724
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270726
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Anna\, Lakithra
LOCATION:Lakithra (Livathos)\, Kefalonia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Lakithra\, the Livathos village where Byron stayed\, celebrates Agia Anna with vespers and a panigiri in the square on the evening of 24 July\, with a live orchestra and food and wine from the village association. It opens the busiest fortnight of Livathos panigiria: Faraklata has Agia Paraskevi on the 25th and Fragata a Kefalonian glendi on the 26th.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#lakithra-livathos-panigiri-of-agia-anna-lakithra
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#lakithra-livathos-panigiri-of-agia-anna-lakithra
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lesvos-skala-kallonis-panigiri-of-agia-anna-with-decorated-bull-ska-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270724
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270726
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Anna with decorated bull\, Skala Kallonis
LOCATION:Skala Kallonis\, Lesvos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:A week before the sardine festival\, Skala Kallonis keeps Agia Anna (25 July) in the old Lesvos style: icon procession\, a garlanded bull led through the village\, local musicians and kiskek shared on the second day. Smaller and more traditional than the sardine crowds\; combine the two if you are on the island for the week.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#skala-kallonis-panigiri-of-agia-anna-with-decorated-bull-ska
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#skala-kallonis-panigiri-of-agia-anna-with-decorated-bull-ska
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:alonnisos-patitiri-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-patitiri-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Patitiri
LOCATION:Patitiri\, Alonnisos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Agia Paraskevi is the patroness of Alonnisos and her church is in Patitiri\, the port: on the evening of 25 July there is a great vespers and a procession of the icon through the streets and along the harbour\, and the municipality's panigiri follows on the quay with a traditional orchestra (the Verykokkos family violins in 2025) and dancing until the early hours. Liturgy next morning. It is the island's biggest night after 15 August\; ferries arrive right into the party\, so book a room in Patitiri or Votsi.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/alonnisos/#patitiri-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-patitiri
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/alonnisos/#patitiri-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-patitiri
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-kato-meria-kolofana-arkesini-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Kato Meria
LOCATION:Kato Meria (Kolofana / Arkesini)\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The biggest panigiri on Amorgos and one of the biggest in the Cyclades: at the church of Agia Paraskevi in the south of the island\, the Kato Meria villages spend ten days preparing\, slaughter around 150 goats\, and on the evening of 25 July the patatato starts cooking in cauldrons for about 4\,000 people who eat free at long tables on the 26th and dance to violins until morning. Bring a car or arrange a lift from Katapola\; there is no bus back at 4 a.m.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#kato-meria-kolofana-arkesini-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#kato-meria-kolofana-arkesini-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chania-vamos-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-vamos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Vamos
LOCATION:Vamos\, Crete (Chania)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Apokoronas market village celebrates its Agia Paraskevi on the evening of 25 July at the springs of Pigadia below the village\, with a Cretan kompania (lyra\, laouto)\, grilled meat and wine\, and dancing until late\; the liturgy is next morning. Parking is on the road into Vamos\, so arrive before 9 pm.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#vamos-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-vamos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#vamos-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-vamos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:corfu-ypsos-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-ypsos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270728
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Ypsos
LOCATION:Ypsos\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The resort village of Ypsos keeps a real three-day panigiri around its church of Agia Paraskevi: vespers at 8pm on the 25th\, liturgy with artoklasia on the 26th and a supplication at 7:30pm\, and each night a big open-air dining area behind the church with the Faiakes orchestra playing Corfiot and Greek dance music. Free entry\, pay for food and drink\; it is on the main coast road so buses from town run late.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#ypsos-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-ypsos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#ypsos-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-ypsos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-karkinagri-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-karkinagri-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Karkinagri
LOCATION:Karkinagri\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:One of the season's busiest nights\, in several villages at once. The Ikarian formula in full: no stage\, no tickets — communal tables of goat in tomato sauce\, soufiko and kathoura cheese\, barrels of village wine\, and live violin-and-lute until dawn.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#karkinagri-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-karkinagri
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#karkinagri-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-karkinagri
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kefalonia-faraklata-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-faraklata-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Faraklata
LOCATION:Faraklata\, Kefalonia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Faraklata\, on the hill road between Argostoli and Sami\, throws its panigiri for Agia Paraskevi on the eve\, 25 July: vespers\, then an orchestra in the square\, grilled meat\, pies and wine until late. Ten minutes from Argostoli\, popular with the town crowd\, so the square fills by 10pm.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#faraklata-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-faraklata
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#faraklata-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-faraklata
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lemnos-thanos-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-thanos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Thanos
LOCATION:Thanos\, Lemnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Thanos\, the village behind the best beaches south of Myrina\, keeps Agia Paraskevi with vespers on 25 July and liturgy on the 26th at its parish church\, followed by the village's summer feast. Myrina's own big church feast of Agios Panteleimon runs the same weekend (26-27 July). Easy from any Myrina hotel.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#thanos-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-thanos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#thanos-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-thanos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-pollonia-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-pollonia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Pollonia
LOCATION:Pollonia\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Pollonia's fishing-village feast: vespers at Agia Paraskevi on the evening of 25 July\, then a free musical evening from about 21:30 with island music\, organised by the Pollonia cultural and beautification society. Crowds are a mix of locals and visitors staying in the village\; book a table at one of the harbour tavernas beforehand\, because they fill up on the night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#pollonia-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-pollonia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#pollonia-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-pollonia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-kinidaros-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kinidaros-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Kinidaros
LOCATION:Kinidaros\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kinidaros\, the marble-quarry village famous for having the most tavernas per head on Naxos\, feasts Agia Paraskevi on the evening of 25 July with grilled meat\, wine and raki and violins in the square. The village also celebrates the Holy Cross on 14 September and Agios Nikolaos on 6 December in the same style.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#kinidaros-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kinidaros
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#kinidaros-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kinidaros
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rhodes-kattavia-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-agios-panteleimon-kattav-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270728
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi & Agios Panteleimon\, Kattavia
LOCATION:Kattavia\, Rhodes\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The southernmost village of Rhodes runs a three-day panigiri from 25 to 27 July for both Agia Paraskevi and Agios Panteleimon\, with a glendi on the square each night and the Prasonisi kitesurf crowd mixing with the locals. Kattavia also feasts the Panagia on 14 August and holds a 'lopou' (local pulse) festival in late August. It is an hour and a half from Rhodes town\, so stay in Gennadi or Lachania rather than driving back.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#kattavia-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-agios-panteleimon-kattav
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#kattavia-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-agios-panteleimon-kattav
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:serifos-kato-chora-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Kato Chora
LOCATION:Kato Chora\, Serifos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Chora feast of high summer: vespers at Agia Paraskevi in Kato Chora on the evening of 25 July\, then food and wine from the ktitores and island dancing (syrto) in the lanes until late\, with liturgy next morning\; a second Agia Paraskevi feast is held at Galani the same night. Chora is car-free — park at the top by the windmills or below at Livadi and take the steps.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#kato-chora-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#kato-chora-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skiathos-platanias-agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-platania-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Platanias
LOCATION:Platanias (Agia Paraskevi)\, Skiathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The municipality's main summer panigiri: vespers at 8 pm on 25 July at the chapel of Agia Paraskevi behind Platanias beach\, then from about 9 pm a live nisiotika orchestra\, dancing and food and drink in the churchyard until late. The 2026 edition was run by the Dimos Skiathou with free entry. It is on the main road to Koukounaries\, so take the bus from town rather than fighting for parking.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#platanias-agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-platania
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#platanias-agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-platania
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:spetses-agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-agia-paraskevi-bea-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Agia Paraskevi beach
LOCATION:Agia Paraskevi\, Spetses\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The pine-fringed bay of Agia Paraskevi on the west coast has a small church of the saint\, and on the night of 25-26 July the island's summer panigiri is held there with food\, live music and dancing until the early hours. No cars on Spetses: go by the round-the-island boat\, a rented scooter or a horse-carriage\, and arrange the return in advance.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-agia-paraskevi-bea
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-agia-paraskevi-bea
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-katapola-psimeni-raki-festival-katapola-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Psimeni Raki Festival\, Katapola
LOCATION:Katapola\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 26 July the harbour square of Katapola celebrates the island's honey-and-spice raki: you watch it being made\, a boat arrives with dancers in costume\, the musicians meet them on the quay\, and everyone is handed psimeni raki\, pasteli and anevates (raki cheese pies) before the dancing goes on into the small hours. It clashes with the Agia Paraskevi feast the same night\, so locals pick one\; Katapola is the easier one without a car.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#katapola-psimeni-raki-festival-katapola
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#katapola-psimeni-raki-festival-katapola
END:VEVENT
