BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:evia-central-chalkida-fair-pazari-of-agia-paraskevi-chalkida-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270802
SUMMARY:Fair (Pazari) of Agia Paraskevi\, Chalkida
LOCATION:Chalkida\, Evia (Central)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Chalkida's patron is Agia Paraskevi\, whose historic basilica is in the Kastro quarter\; her feast on 26 July opens a week-long fair established by royal decree in 1864\, with hundreds of stalls\, street food and rides\, held since 2026 in the Parko tou Laou (26 July-1 August in 2026) after decades in Vourkos. Vespers and a procession on the 25th at the church\; the fair is at its liveliest after 9 pm. Park at the municipal pool.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-central/#chalkida-fair-pazari-of-agia-paraskevi-chalkida
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-central/#chalkida-fair-pazari-of-agia-paraskevi-chalkida
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:folegandros-ano-meria-panigiri-of-agios-panteleimon-ano-meria-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270728
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Panteleimon\, Ano Meria
LOCATION:Ano Meria\, Folegandros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The big feast of Ano Meria\, the farming village strung along the ridge west of Chora\, for its 'miracle-working' Agios Panteleimon: vespers on the evening of 26 July\, then food and wine from the households\, violin and laouto and dancing in front of the church\, with liturgy on the 27th. It is the island's largest panigiri after Easter\; the bus runs late that night\, and the matsata (hand-made pasta) tavernas of Ano Meria are the place to eat first.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#ano-meria-panigiri-of-agios-panteleimon-ano-meria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#ano-meria-panigiri-of-agios-panteleimon-ano-meria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:heraklion-kounavoi-panigiri-of-agios-panteleimon-kounavoi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270728
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Panteleimon\, Kounavoi
LOCATION:Kounavoi\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:In the Peza wine country fifteen kilometres from Heraklion\, Kounavoi celebrates Agios Panteleimon at its country chapel on the evening of 26 July with a Cretan glenti\, local wine from the cooperatives and food from the village association. It is a locals' panigiri that visitors staying in Heraklion can reach by taxi in twenty minutes.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#kounavoi-panigiri-of-agios-panteleimon-kounavoi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#kounavoi-panigiri-of-agios-panteleimon-kounavoi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-agios-panteleimonas-panigiri-of-agios-panteleimon-agios-pant-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270728
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Panteleimon\, Agios Panteleimonas (Agios Kirykos)
LOCATION:Agios Panteleimonas\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The hamlet named after the saint\, just above Agios Kirykos\, hosts the feast on the evening of 26 July in the church courtyard\, and comes back on 27 August for Agios Fanourios with the Zelepos orchestra. Feidos (Evdilos side) and Myrsonas (Raches) keep Agios Panteleimon the same night. Easy one to reach from town by car or taxi.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#agios-panteleimonas-panigiri-of-agios-panteleimon-agios-pant
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#agios-panteleimonas-panigiri-of-agios-panteleimon-agios-pant
